Okay, here’s a Mermaid’s Lullaby, designed to be comforting for a child through a storm, incorporating the elements and a gentle rhythm.  I’ve aimed for a soothing, slightly mystical feel.

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[Storm's Embrace, a Gentle Sigh] --> B(The Waves Do Roar, a Wildly Deep);
    B --> C{Raindrops Fall, a Silver Sleep};
    C --> D(The Wind Does Whisper, a Secret Keep);
    D --> E[The Dock Lights Gleam, a Safe Retreat];

    B --> F(Darkness Falls, a Shadow's Grace);
    F --> G(The Fog Does Curl, a Quiet Space);
    G --> H(Stars Begin to Shine, a Gentle Pace);

    H --> I[Little One, don’t you fear; 
     The Storm Will Pass, a Sweetly Clear 
     And Calmness Will Come, so near. 
     Let Dreams of Silver Drift, like Tears];

    style A fill:#f9f,stroke:#333,stroke-width:2px
    style B fill:#ccf,stroke:#333,stroke-width:2px
    style C fill:#fff,stroke:#333,stroke-width:2px
    style D fill:#fff,stroke:#333,stroke-width:2px
    style E fill:#fff,stroke:#333,stroke-width:2px
    style F fill:#eee,stroke:#333,stroke-width:2px
    style G fill:#eee,stroke:#333,stroke-width:2px
    style H fill:#eee,stroke:#333,stroke-width:2px
    style I fill:#f9f,stroke:#333,stroke-width:2px
```

**Explanation and Notes:**

*   **Mermaid Syntax:** This is a standard Mermaid syntax.  You can copy and paste this code into a Mermaid editor (like the one on the Mermaid Live Editor: [https://mermaid.live/](https://mermaid.live/)) to see the visual representation.
